💡 Key Takeaways

    Pattern recognition: High disk utilization with low actual data transfer pointed to maintenance jobs, not hardware failure
    Timing matters: Backup and cleanup tasks scheduled during startup create cascading delays
    Recovery ≠ done: Post-filesystem-repair settings often need manual tuning to prevent recurring slowdowns
    Transparency in troubleshooting: Documenting every diagnostic step makes future problems faster to resolve
